.TH LOOM 1 "June 2026" "loom 0.3.7" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
loom \- unified agentic ecosystem for sharing skills, sessions, and MCP servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B loom
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B loom
is a single CLI front\-end for an ecosystem of agentic coding tools
(claude\-code, jcode, crush, opencode, goose, and others).
.PP
It manages a shared directory at
.BR ~/.loom/
that contains discovered skills, MCP server configurations, session
exports, authentication credentials, hooks, and a knowledge graph, so
that the same context is available to every tool the developer
launches.
.PP
A background daemon,
.BR loomd (1),
aggregates the per\-crate subsystems and exposes them over a Unix
domain socket; the CLI connects to the daemon when one is running, or
runs a small subset of operations standalone.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Lifecycle
.TP
.B init
Initialize the
.B ~/.loom/
ecosystem directory.  Accepts
.B \-\-import
to scan the local filesystem and
.B \-\-recommended
to install the recommended set of MCP servers.
.TP
.B scan
Print a summary of the resources currently registered with the
ecosystem.
.TP
.B status
Show ecosystem and daemon health.
.TP
.B doctor
Run deep diagnostics for the daemon, service installation, and
persistence layer.
.TP
.B tui
Launch the terminal UI dashboard (seven tabs, 1s auto refresh).
.SS Tool and integration management
.TP
.B thread \fItool\fR
Register or update an agentic tool.  Accepts
.B \-\-apply\-routing \fIdecision\fR
to immediately adopt a routing decision.
.TP
.B exec \fItools...\fR
Execute one or more tools with the Loom ecosystem loaded.
.TP
.B init\-shell \fI[\-\-shell bash|zsh|fish]\fR
Generate shell integration that activates Loom on
.BR cd .
.TP
.B add\-acp\-agent \fIagent_id\fR
Pull an agent entry from the public ACP registry and add it locally.
.TP
.B sync
Sync Loom\-managed resources to tool\-native filesystem locations.
.SS Subsystems
.TP
.B mcp
Manage MCP servers (\fBlist\fR, \fBshow\fR, \fBadd\fR, \fBremove\fR,
\fBinstall\fR, \fBlist\-known\fR).
.TP
.B skills
Manage skills (\fBlist\fR, \fBshow\fR, \fBinstall\fR, \fBremove\fR).
.TP
.B sessions
Manage session exports (\fBlist\fR, \fBshow\fR, \fBexport\fR,
\fBimport\fR, \fBresume\fR, \fBsearch\fR, \fBrecall\fR, \fBindex\fR,
\fBbranch\fR, \fBtag\fR, \fBtags\fR, \fBsummarize\fR).  Resumption
can inject memory and knowledge entities.  \fBrecall\fR groups
matching messages by session, returning the top sessions (hit
count + best match) for a query.  \fBtag\fR mutates a session's
tag set (\fB--add\fR/\fB--remove\fR); \fBtags\fR lists every distinct
tag in the index.  \fBlist\fR, \fBsearch\fR, and \fBrecall\fR all
accept \fB--tag\fR to filter to sessions whose tag set intersects
the given set.  \fBsummarize\fR auto-compresses a session once its
message count exceeds the compression threshold (default 20):
older messages are folded into a single System-role summary at the
head of the message list, and the last 10 messages are kept
verbatim; auto-runs on \fBappend_message\fR once a session crosses
the threshold.  \fB--force\fR re-runs even when the session is
already at or below the threshold.
.TP
.B auth
Manage authentication providers and the encrypted credential vault.
.TP
.B hooks
Manage event hooks (\fBlist\fR, \fBshow\fR, \fBregister\fR,
\fBremove\fR, \fBrun\fR, \fBverify\fR).  Supported event types include
\fBPreToolUse\fR, \fBPostToolUse\fR, \fBUserPromptSubmit\fR, and
\fBPostPhase\fR (fired after a workflow phase completes).
.TP
.B workflow
Manage workflow tasks (\fBlist\fR, \fBshow\fR, \fBcreate\fR,
\fBadvance\fR, \fBassign\fR, \fBdispatch\fR).  The \fBdispatch\fR
subcommand accepts
.B \-\-auto\-advance
which runs every phase of a task back to back, capturing each
phase's result and passing it to the next phase as the
.B LOOM_PRIOR_PHASE_RESULT
environment variable.
.TP
.B routing
Inspect and override the complexity\-scoring based model router
(\fBshow\fR, \fBevaluate\fR, \fBscore\fR, \fBrecommend\fR,
\fBoverride\fR, \fBcatalog\fR).
.TP
.B knowledge
Build and query the SQLite knowledge graph (\fBbuild\fR,
\fBquery\fR, \fBstats\fR, \fBadd\fR, \fBrelate\fR, \fBsearch\fR).
.TP
.B memory
Manage the AgentMemory persistent memory server.
.TP
.B issues
Manage the issue tracker integration (currently GitHub Issues).
.TP
.B lock
Manage the skill lock file used to pin skill versions for
reproducibility.
.TP
.B plugin
Manage the plugin registry (\fBsearch\fR, \fBinstall\fR,
\fBupdate\fR, \fBremove\fR).
.SS Daemon
.TP
.B daemon \fIstart|stop|status|restart\fR
Manage the background
.BR loomd (1)
process.
.TP
.B daemon install\-service
Install
.B loomd
as a user\-level launchd service.
.TP
.B daemon uninstall\-service
Remove the launchd service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the Loom version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LOOM_TASK_ID
Set during hook script execution to the current workflow task id.
.TP
.B LOOM_PHASE
Set during hook script execution to the current workflow phase.
.TP
.B LOOM_AGENT
Set during hook script execution to the current agent identifier.
.TP
.B LOOM_EXIT_CODE
Set during \fBPostPhase\fR hook execution to the agent's exit code.
.TP
.B LOOM_EXPECTED_RESULT_PATH
Set during workflow dispatch to the path the agent should write its
result file to.
.TP
.B LOOM_PRIOR_PHASE_RESULT
Set during workflow dispatch to the JSON of the most recent phase
result, when one exists.
.TP
.B LOOM_DIR
Override the location of the Loom data directory (default
.BR ~/.loom/ ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.loom/
The shared ecosystem directory.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/loomd.sock
The daemon's Unix domain IPC socket.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/workflow/tasks/
Workflow task manifests and per\-phase result files.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/hooks/
Hook configuration files and scripts.
.TP
.B ~/.loom/knowledge/graph.db
The SQLite knowledge graph.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The CLI exits 0 on success and non\-zero on error.  When
\fBdispatch\fR is invoked with \fB\-\-auto\-advance\fR, the first
non\-zero agent exit code propagates as the CLI exit code and aborts
the phase chain.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loomd (1)
.PP
Project home: <https://github.com/tusharmewara/loom>
